      "reviewer_name": "Anonymous",
      "rating": null,
      "title": "iworks fine, sound leaves something to be desired",
      "review_text": "my only issue is there's no way to adjust the bass - it must be set really strong for CDs because the low tones growl when the volume is turned up and the left speaker vibrates like it's loose on some of my CDs. It's got a good radio with strong reception from the little antenna on stations 75 miles away, but happens to sound more treble than I like. So CDs too low, radio too high. A neat feature is the manual radio dial on the side being upside down so it's easy to bend over and see the numbers without having to lift it up to eye level. I prefer the old-fashioned radio dial over digital. The dials and buttons all feel very solid and are easy to navigate, and it feels like a good sturdy compact player that hopefully will last a long time. My two big Sony boomboxes only lasted a couple of years each before starting to skip (only playing 1 hour per day) and cleaners didn't help. Jensen has always been a very reliable brand and if you are wanting a basic CD player and radio without lots of bells and whistles and studio sound, this might be just the ticket for you. I was happy to find it at Walmart at such a great price.",
